      {
        "id": 151277,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-06T21:19:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Prevention is at the same timing as Redirection. Thus it gives the choice. Prevention is in no way the same as damage Immunity or being unable to deal damage. How do we know this? Take Null Point Callibration Unit, if Meteor Storm is in play and he tries to deal hismelf Cold damage, it would not work. Same if Absolute Zero is suffering from the effects of Ensnaring Brambles. Null-Point Callibration Unit also takes place after damage type, say Imbued Fire is in play you will be unable to deal Absolute Zero Cold damage and thus not trigger it. Null-Point Callibration also factors in Damage Modifiers, so it can be reduced to 0 and actually be unable to trigger or it can be increased so it makes it a higher amount of healing. Effects like Meteor Storm and Ensnaring Brambles will not trigger any of these things because they are before them and stop them from working. This is exactly why Undaunted, Null-Point Callibration Unit, Flak Jacket, and any other cards that can prevent damage can occur at the same time as redirection cards.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:30:05.264Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
